# Response headers, in the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format.
#
# Header support is entirely the host's. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this
# file; plain S3, nginx and GitHub Pages do not, and simply serve it as one more
# static asset. public/ is copied verbatim into dist/, so it ships on every
# build either way — which means its presence in the repo proves nothing about
# whether the live site sends these. Check the response headers in DevTools
# after a deploy rather than assuming this took.
#
# Why each of the four, and why each is safe to ship without testing:
#
#   X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#     Stops a browser second-guessing a declared Content-Type. Everything here
#     is a static asset served with the type the host derived from its
#     extension, so nothing on the site depends on sniffing.
#
#   Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
#     Every page pulls Google Fonts, and / and /media embed youtube-nocookie.
#     Under the browser default those third parties are handed the full URL,
#     which on this site names the exact fund, AMC or SEBI category page a
#     visitor was reading. They get the bare origin instead; same-origin
#     requests still carry the full URL, so nothing internal changes.
#
#   X-Frame-Options: DENY
#     Nobody may put this site in a frame. The four forms collect name, phone,
#     city and ARN — exactly what a clickjacking overlay exists to harvest.
#     This governs who may frame us, not whom we may frame: the
#     youtube-nocookie iframes on / and /media are unaffected.
#
#   Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
#     No page asks for a camera, a microphone or a location. Denying them now
#     means a third-party script added later cannot quietly start asking.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content-Security-Policy — deliberately NOT enabled, and NOT verified.
#
# The draft below is a starting point, not a working policy. It has never been
# served and has never been tested against a real page load. Do not uncomment it
# until someone has loaded every route with it in report-only mode
# (Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only) and read the console. A CSP that breaks
# this site is worse than no CSP: it fails closed and silently, and the first
# symptom is a dead lead form.
#
# What a working policy has to allow. Verified against the source on 2026-09-08;
# file names rather than line numbers, because these files move.
#
#   'unsafe-inline' for scripts — src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro and five pages
#     (pages/index, pages/explore, pages/compare, pages/amc/index,
#     pages/funds/venture-capital) use <script is:inline>, and BaseLayout emits
#     the JSON-LD graph as <script type="application/ld+json">. None of them
#     carry a nonce or a hash, so a policy without 'unsafe-inline' kills the
#     nav, the explore filters, the comparison table and the structured data at
#     once. Moving to nonces means changing how those blocks are emitted — real
#     work, not a header edit.
#
#   'unsafe-inline' for styles — nine source files use style="..." attributes
#     (the material-symbols font-variation-settings overrides among them), and
#     BaseLayout.astro ships a <noscript><style> block for the icon font.
#
#   https://fonts.googleapis.com in style-src — the two stylesheet <link>s in
#     BaseLayout.astro: Cormorant Garamond / Manrope / Newsreader, and Material
#     Symbols Outlined.
#
#   https://fonts.gstatic.com in font-src — the font files those two
#     stylesheets then request.
#
#   https://api.web3forms.com in connect-src — where all four forms deliver;
#     see SITE.form.endpoint in src/config/site.ts. Every form posts by fetch()
#     from public/site-interactive.js and no <form> in src/ carries an action
#     attribute, so this belongs in connect-src and form-action stays 'self'.
#
#   https://www.youtube-nocookie.com in frame-src — the playlist embeds on
#     src/pages/index.astro and src/pages/media.astro.
#
# Draft, untested:
#
# /*
#   Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
#
# img-src omits data: because the build emits no data: URIs today — Astro writes
# every processed image to /_astro/. Re-check that before enabling; an inlined
# image would fail closed with nothing but a console line to show for it.
